.TH XPN-SERVER-SETUP 8 "October 2026" "XPN 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
xpn-server-setup \- configure or migrate the packaged XPN server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xpn-server-setup --url
.I https://host/xpn
.RB [ --migrate-checkout ]
.RB [ --plan ]
.RB [ --host-tcp-ports " 22,443" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Configure XPN in an existing nginx HTTPS site. Generate credentials only on
first installation; preserve existing device accounts, keys and settings.
Start the non-root control and packet services and configure TUN/NAT.
Reruns update only changed resources. Root access is required for installation.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --plan
Read-only preview; do not change files or start services.
.TP
.B --migrate-checkout
Explicitly migrate a checkout managed by the XPN installer to the package units.
Back up and remove managed local unit overrides; preserve database and settings.
.TP
.B --nginx-site PATH
Select an existing nginx HTTPS site when auto-detection is ambiguous.
.TP
.B --certificate PATH
Select its PEM certificate when it is in a separate included file.
.TP
.B --control-port PORT, --native-port PORT
Select unprivileged loopback backend ports for a new installation.
.TP
.B --host-tcp-ports LIST
Comma-separated server TCP ports accessible inside the VPN. Reruns preserve it.
.TP
.B --show-admin-token
Print the administrator token locally. Do not capture in shared logs.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/xpn.env
.br
.I /etc/xpn/install.json
.br
.I /var/lib/xpn
.br
.I /var/backups/xpn
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xpn (1)
